# Gitignored files copied into every worktree Claude Code creates
# (--worktree, subagent worktrees, desktop parallel sessions).
#
# Syntax is .gitignore's, but the rule is narrower: a pattern only takes effect
# if the file it matches is ALSO gitignored. Tracked files are never duplicated.
#
# `.env` carries local overrides the Makefile `-include`s. A fresh worktree has
# none, so a build there would silently lose whatever it sets. Treat as
# credential-bearing: never paste it, never commit it.
.env

# MCP server enablement and the permission allowlist. Without it a worktree
# session prompts for tool calls the main checkout allows, which stalls an
# unattended run.
.claude/settings.local.json

# A contributor's signing overrides, pulled in with `#include?`. The `?` makes
# it optional, so a worktree without it builds cleanly and without iCloud.
Configs/Local.xcconfig

# Apple's skills, which are local copies and not in the repository.
.claude/skills/audit-xcode-security-settings/
.claude/skills/swiftui-specialist/
.claude/skills/swiftui-whats-new-27/
